Clamp the same integer prescale in the ten upstream files the catalogue reaches.

These ten carry the bug that blackened crt-aperture and sharp-bilinear, and none of
them is in the bundle: they exist only in the pinned slang-shaders tree the downloadable
catalogue is built from. That is why this is a second patch. The first one,
slang-shaders-prescale-zero-guard.patch, records the two bundled files and reverses at
the repository root. This one cannot: there is nothing here to reverse. Reverse it inside
a slang-shaders checkout instead:

    git apply -R -p9 platforms/ios/patches/slang-shaders-catalogue-prescale-zero-guard.patch

The path prefix on every hunk is a strip-level convention, not a claim that these files
live under assets/. shader_manifest.py finds a patch by that prefix and applies it with
-p9, so the prefix has to be there for the generator to see the file at all.

Each shader derives a whole-number scale from output size over source size, then divides
by it. RetroArch feeds them a small console framebuffer, so the ratio never falls below
one. PCSX2 renders internally at up to 8x, so above roughly 1.5x the source is taller
than the screen, floor() returns zero and the divide yields NaN.

Ten files, twelve sites, 98 presets unblocked. Twelve and not ten because the scanner
reports one site per file: clamping the first in crt-potato and ultra_potato made a second
visible in each, in the mask size their fragment stage divides a texture coordinate by.
Every clamp was written against the site the scanner named, then the scan was run again
until it came back empty.

Each file also gains a five-line notice under its #version line. A catalogue zip travels
on its own: whoever installs one gets the bytes and never sees the manifest's per-file
modified record, so GPL section 2(a)'s prominent notice has to be in the file itself.

Two of the ten clamp the composed value rather than the floor() alone. retro-tiles adds
OVERSCAN afterwards, which a preset can set to -3, and bead picks between the floor and a
user scale. Clamping only the floor would leave a second route to zero in both, one that
has nothing to do with upscaling and is reachable at any resolution.

Two more are copies of crt-aperture living elsewhere in the tree under other names, and
one of those is a .h. That is why test_ios_shader_prescale_guard.py scans .inc and .h and
not only .slang.

Of the ten, four are reachable from a preset the signed licence rules actually offer, and
those four are what 73 of the catalogue's presets rest on. The other six are clamped
anyway: the class rules can change, and the generator's prescale gate has to come back
empty for the run to be trustworthy at all.

Signed off with the whole-tree catalogue on 2026-08-18. shader_manifest.py records every
file here as modified, with its upstream and served hashes.

